is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: router6
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: the host firewall (iptables) on the site’s default gateway, router6, specifically the forwarding policy on its WAN-facing interface eth2 (10.50.1.2) toward router3 (10.50.1.1).

Mechanism: Clients on 172.18.51.0/24 can reach the gateway (172.18.51.254) reliably, but any traffic that leaves the site toward “the internet” (via eth2) has its return packets dropped by router6’s FORWARD chain. The rules include blanket drops for any packet entering on eth2, so replies from upstream are discarded, making user sessions appear to “hiccup” or hang simultaneously for all four users.

Localization: Router6 eth1 serves the LAN (172.18.51.254/24) and eth2 connects upstream (10.50.1.2/24). Evidence:
- From a L
